The paper’s Step-0 discriminator rules out its positive graph classes for Track A: tame classes are polynomial via minimal-separator enumeration (Theorem 4), and the paper explicitly constructs TJ sequences for series-parallel graphs. The viable native regime is instead Section 4’s peanut-like bipartite graphs, where separator reconfiguration is exactly complement-dual to bipartite independent-set reconfiguration and is NP-complete under TJ/TAR (Lemma 3, Theorem 3, Corollary 1). I’m now checking whether a planted yes-distribution in that regime survives the natural reconfiguration search, rather than relying on worst-case NP-hardness alone.
