   310	    Now, suppose $s = u$.
   311	    If $t = v$ or there is some $e_i = st$, a similar argument to the one used for sequential pairs holds: in the first case, $V(s,t)$ is a minimum separator of size $\varepsilon(s,t) + 1$, in the second, $V(s,t) \cup (\supp(t) \setminus \{s\})$ is a minimum separator of size $\varepsilon(s,t) + 2$.
