codex
The paper’s decisive split is now clear: TJ/TAR is NP-complete on the paper’s peanut-like bipartite graphs, TS is PSPACE-complete there, while tame classes, chordal graphs, `{3P1, diamond}`-free graphs, and series-parallel graphs are explicitly easy. I’m therefore exploring the paper-licensed bipartite reduction under token sliding; the certificate will be a replayable move sequence generated first, then hidden by construction.
